# G059 — Patient-Doctor Scheduler

*v2. See `patient-doctor-scheduler.md` for prose: three-way conflict check
(doctor, room, patient), find-slot as cost-budgeted search, rescheduling
as transactional update.*

---

## Choreographic Case: Urgent Slot Request

[find-next-available @doctor-id @duration @within-start @within-end @patient-id
    IN ORDER TO
        find the soonest available slot for an urgent appointment
        with both doctor and room resource conflict checks
        and notify both patient and resource desk before committing

    @slot <- [scheduler[find-slot {doctor-id: @doctor-id,
                                     duration: @duration,
                                     from: @within-start,
                                     until: @within-end,
                                     step: 15-min}]]
             || -> #no-slot-in-window

    concurrent [
        <- @sarah{notify patient: @patient-id, slot: @slot}
        <- @kathryn{confirm room and resources for: @slot}
    ]
    join

    @appt <- [scheduler[schedule {patient: @patient-id,
                                    doctor: @doctor-id,
                                    room: @slot:room,
                                    start: @slot:time,
                                    end: @slot:time + @duration}]]
             || -> #booking-lost-to-race @resistance:reason

    -> @appt
]

---

## Verb Surface

[scheduler
    new
    add-doctor          {doctor}
    add-room            {room}
    schedule            {patient, doctor, room, start, end}    ;; || conflict
    cancel              {id}
    reschedule          {id, new-start, new-end, new-room?}    ;; || conflict
    doctor-conflicts    {doctor-id, start, end, except?}
    room-conflicts      {room-id, start, end, except?}
    find-slot           {doctor-id, duration, from, until, step?}
    doctor-schedule     {doctor-id}
    room-schedule       {room-id}
    patient-history     {patient-id}
]

---

## Distinctive Innate idiom: conflict check as `<-` verification

[scheduler[schedule {patient: @p, doctor: @d, room: @r, start: @s, end: @e}]
    <- [scheduler[doctor-conflicts {doctor-id: @d, start: @s, end: @e}]]
        where result is empty
    <- [scheduler[room-conflicts {room-id: @r, start: @s, end: @e}]]
        where result is empty
    || -> #conflict-detected

Multiple `<-` verification gates compose: each must pass before
advance. A failure at either surfaces the exact conflict source.

---

## Demo

[demo
    @sch <- [scheduler[new]]
    [scheduler[add-doctor {doctor: {id: "D-CHEN", name: "Dr Chen",
                                      specialty: "cardiology"}}]]
    [scheduler[add-room   {room: {id: "R-1", capacity: 1}}]]

    @slot <- [scheduler[find-slot {doctor-id: "D-CHEN",
                                    duration: 30-min,
                                    from: @today-9am,
                                    until: @today-5pm,
                                    step: 15-min}]]
    -> @slot                       ;; -> (9:00, "R-1")

    @appt <- [scheduler[schedule {patient: "P-101",
                                    doctor: "D-CHEN",
                                    room: @slot:room,
                                    start: @slot:time,
                                    end: @slot:time + 30-min}]]
    -> @appt:id                    ;; -> assigned id

    ;; Try to double-book; resistance expected
    [scheduler[schedule {patient: "P-102",
                          doctor: "D-CHEN",
                          room: "R-1",
                          start: @appt:start,
                          end: @appt:end}]]
        || -> "doctor-conflict"
]
